.SH EXIT STATUS
.IP 0
    Successful pipeline execution and all commands terminated with code 0
.IP 1
    An error occured
.IP "<child exit code>"
    The return code from a command, if pipeline executed successfully but at least
    one command exited with non-zero return code.
.IP "128 + <signal number>"
    If pipeline executed successfully but a command was terminated by a signal.
    Exit status is the signal number added to the constant 128.
    Could also mean that
.BR mexec " itself was terminated by a signal."
.PP
In case multiple commands returned non-zero exit code or were terminated by a signal
it is indeterminate which code was propagated as the exit status.
.PP
Note that it may not be possible to distinguish between a child exit code 1 or
an error setting up the pipeline. Likewise it may also not be possible to
distinguish between a child exit code larger than 128 and a signal termination code.

